  <metadata>
    <name>Wae Rebo out-and-back</name>
    <desc>Wae Rebo out-and-back (alternative): If the onward trail from Wae Rebo cannot be done with a bike: climb to the village, descend the same path to Denge, then ride the remote-profile road to Todo. 60.2 km, +2018 m. Replaces 60.1 km / +2018 m of the main course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:58Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.808000" lon="120.302000">
    <ele>481.4</ele>
    <name>Denge</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: trailhead | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay | position approximate -- Last village reachable by road/motorbike before the Wae Rebo trek (about 8 km, +700 m, 2.5-3 h on foot). Coordinates placed by interpolation from route descriptions (~6 km from Dintor, ~7-9 km from Wae Rebo) and cross-ch</desc>
    <sym>Trail Head</sym>
    <type>anchor/trailhead</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.770000" lon="120.284170">
    <ele>1115.9</ele>
    <name>Wae Rebo</name>
    <desc>km 14.6 | kind: checkpoint | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- Cultural checkpoint; UNESCO Asia-Pacific award village. All visitors sleep and eat inside the mbaru niang under the village's own homestay system -- a race stop here means income for the community by design. Requires an </desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>anchor/checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.730920" lon="120.381590">
    <ele>464.5</ele>
    <name>Todo</name>
    <desc>km 60.2 | kind: village | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: none -- Former seat of the Manggarai kingdom; day-trip village, no lodging found. Confirmed by five independent Overture/OSM points (church, clinic, tourism tag, school) clustered within 1.5 km.</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.730920" lon="120.381590">
    <ele>464.5</ele>
    <name>Todo</name>
    <desc>[anchor] Former seat of the Manggarai kingdom, with the oldest mbaru niang (conical drum house) in the regency and a genealogy said to trace Manggarai's first king; a day-trip village, not set up for overnight stays.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.770000" lon="120.284170">
    <ele>1115.9</ele>
    <name>Wae Rebo</name>
    <desc>[anchor, hike-a-bike] Seven cone-shaped mbaru niang houses ringing a mountain clearing at ~1,100-1,200 m, reached only on foot; winner of the 2012 UNESCO Asia-Pacific Award for Cultural Heritage Conservation. Flores' most famous traditional village and the race's flagship cultural checkpoint.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>Wae Rebo out-and-back</name>
    <desc>Wae Rebo out-and-back (alternative): If the onward trail from Wae Rebo cannot be done with a bike: climb to the village, descend the same path to Denge, then ride the remote-profile road to Todo. 60.2 km, +2018 m. Replaces 60.1 km / +2018 m of the main course.</desc>
